> worth more as a light source.  Castle wand supposed to be non-
> rechargable.  Fair enough.  When I got there, it was 1:0.  Had to
> wrest it to get my cloak of MR.  I'm feeling very abused by now.

Interesting. Less wishes -> feeling abused? A wishless NetHack game
would be similar abusive in that case?

> Thrones don't give wishes either.  Why doesn't the author just remove
> wishes from the game entirely?

Because I think wishes are useful. They help you save time when you
need a certain item and don't want to wait for the death drop. If you
have a /oW at 1:1 you can wish up a lifesaver in a dire situation.

But in vanilla you get dozens of wishes. Wishes should be precious and
rare.

That's why I removed wishes from thrones (what was the motivation for
that anyway?), limited djinn to non-magical items and decreased the
initial charging of /oW.

